<title>EGYPT: Egypt says seeks 25,000 tonnes palm oils.</title>
<headline>Egypt says seeks 25,000 tonnes palm oils.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's official Holding Company for Food Industries said on Tuesday it was seeking 25,000 tonnes of Malaysian and/or Indonesian palm stearin and palm oil for delivery in August.</p>
<p>Moharram Ghanem, head of the sales sector, told Reuters the deadline for bids was 0900 GMT on June 25. He said he wanted the oils in the following lots:</p>
<p>-- 10,000 tonnes of palm stearin</p>
<p>-- 15,000 tonnes of palm oil.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1 mf me</p>
</text>
